## Vercel Speed Insights Installation - Implementation Report

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the G11 IPL Fantasy League project.

### What was implemented:

**1. Package Installation**
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 using npm
- Package added to dependencies in package.json
- Updated package-lock.json to reflect the new dependency

**2. Component Integration**
- Added SpeedInsights component to the root layout file (src/app/layout.tsx)
- Imported from `@vercel/speed-insights/next` (Next.js App Router specific import)
- Placed the component alongside the existing Analytics component in the body tag

### Files Modified:

**Created:**
- None (used existing package manager and layout structure)

**Modified:**
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component

### Implementation Details:

This is a Next.js 16.2.1 project using the App Router architecture. I followed the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation (fetched fresh from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart) which specifies:

1. For Next.js App Router projects, the SpeedInsights component should be imported from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
2. The component should be placed in the root layout file
3. The component works alongside the existing Vercel Analytics setup

The implementation follows the project's existing patterns:
- Maintained the existing import organization
- Placed SpeedInsights next to the Analytics component for consistency
- No additional configuration was needed as the component works out-of-the-box

### Testing & Verification:

✅ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
✅ No new linting errors introduced
✅ No TypeScript errors
✅ Lock file properly updated

### Notes:

- The project already had @vercel/analytics installed, so Speed Insights complements the existing analytics setup
- Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance metrics after the next deployment to Vercel
- No environment variables or additional configuration required
- The component is lightweight and won't affect page load performance
